# Context Artifacts

## Goal

Keep short-lived execution memory in explicit runtime artifacts instead of scattering it across chat turns.

## Recommended local runtime files

- `.ai/context/current.md`
- `.ai/context/initiatives/<slug>/issues-manifest.json`
- `{{ plan_progress_runtime_root }}/ISSUE-ID/plan.md` (local `PLAN::ISSUE-ID` mirror)
- `{{ plan_progress_runtime_root }}/ISSUE-ID/progress.md` (local `PROGRESS::ISSUE-ID` mirror)
- `.ai/runtime/orchestrator/registry.json`
- `.ai/runtime/orchestrator/runs/ISSUE-ID.json`
- `.ai/runtime/supervisor/runs/<slug>.json`
- `.ai/runtime/supervisor/current/<slug>.md`

Configured in `ai.config.yaml` as `artifacts.planProgressRoot` (template default: `.ai/context/runtime`).

## `current.md`

Use as a short digest only:

- active scope
- touched files
- adjacent surfaces
- current step
- latest verify evidence

Do not dump large research or full code excerpts into `current.md`.

## Runtime mirrors

If tracker-backed `PLAN::` / `PROGRESS::` artifacts are unavailable — or as a durable local copy while the tracker holds the live comment — write them under the configured root, **one directory per issue**:

- `{{ plan_progress_runtime_root }}/ISSUE-ID/plan.md`
- `{{ plan_progress_runtime_root }}/ISSUE-ID/progress.md`

Use the same markers and body structure as the tracker artifacts (see `.ai/reference/plan-progress-template.md`). Do not use repo-root `docs/ai/` for these; keep plan/progress under `.ai` only.

## Orchestrator runtime

If work is coordinated through `/orchestrator`, the source of truth for reservation, queueing, and worktree ownership is:

- `.ai/runtime/orchestrator/registry.json`
- `.ai/runtime/orchestrator/runs/ISSUE-ID.json`

## Supervisor runtime

If a multi-issue flow is being executed through `supervisor`, the source of truth is:

- `.ai/context/initiatives/<slug>/issues-manifest.json`
- `.ai/runtime/supervisor/runs/<slug>.json`
- `.ai/runtime/supervisor/current/<slug>.md`
